cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "PRISMA: open climate forecast verification, starting with Argentina — operational verification and global 132-station expansion"
type: software
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-11-25"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Akunimal/prisma-climate"
url: "https://akunimal.github.io/prisma-climate/"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24309947
authors:
  - family-names: "Rodríguez Roncoroni"
    given-names: "Inti Sol"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-5082-5877"
abstract: >-
  Open, independent research software for archiving, verifying, and locally
  calibrating numerical weather prediction ensemble forecasts against station
  observations. Implements a frozen verification protocol, fair CRPS scoring,
  ensemble model output statistics (EMOS), quantile mapping, operational
  verification against climatology and persistence, and a reconciled global
  observational network of 132 stations across 8 regions.
keywords:
  - weather-forecasting
  - climate-prediction
  - forecast-verification
  - ensemble-forecasting
  - statistical-postprocessing
  - emos
  - quantile-mapping
  - argentina
